= Ala Rızgari Is Founded

Ala Rızgari are among the Kurdish political organizations established during 1979.

**Rızgarî splits**

Another day, another split in the left. The largely urban, intellectual-focused Rızgarî organisation had long harboured a radical, militant core of youth supporters, who had so far remained compliant with the organisational line of ''mobilisation-by-journal''. It seems with the latest events unfolding, the militant wing has staged a violent split within the organisation. While the Rızgarî magazine itself remains in the hands of the mainline group, most of the organisation's front organisations and youth associations have also split to establish Ala Rızgarî (Liberation Banner/Flag of Liberation).

Ala Rızgarî differs from the mainline organisation mostly on conjuncture-related disagreements. While Rızgarî holds a neutral view on the Soviet Union and also remains neutral regarding the clashes between pro-Talabani and pro-Barzani forces in Iraqi Kurdistan, Ala Rızgarî has adopted a firmly pro-Soviet, pro-Talabani, pro-Armed struggle position. There are reports that the organisation has already began taking a more active and aggressive approach to mass public mobilisation while also cultivating an armed core. In any case, these news are worrying as the turf war between different Kurdish factions causes more and more violence.

